PART OF CANVAS
--------------

SynapsD is the context-based document indexing engine behind Canvas.
It provides context trees, bitmap indexes, document schemas and vector search.

This repository is one component of the Canvas project. It is developed and
released as part of Canvas, but it lives in its own repository:

    this component   https://github.com/canvas-ui/canvas-synapsd
    the project      https://github.com/canvas-ui/canvas-server

Canvas components are not all licensed the same way. The server runtime and the
services it embeds are dual-licensed. The standalone clients are AGPL-only. The
COMPONENTS section of the project NOTICE lists which is which.

NETWORK USE
-----------

This component is a library embedded in canvas-server rather than a network
service of its own, but it forms part of a program that is made available to
users over a network. Section 13 of the AGPL therefore applies to the combined
work. If you run a modified Canvas and let users interact with it over a
network, those users must be able to obtain the corresponding source of your
modifications, including any you make to this component.

canvas-server implements its side of that obligation. Every HTTP response
carries an `X-Source-Code` header, and `GET /rest/v2/ping` (no authentication
required) reports the running version, revision and source URL:

    curl -sI https://your-host/ | grep -i x-source-code
    curl -s  https://your-host/rest/v2/ping

If you deploy a modified version, repoint these at the repository that publishes
your changes. Set `CANVAS_SOURCE_URL`, and set `CANVAS_SOURCE_COMMIT` where the
build has no git metadata. Removing the notice instead of repointing it does not
satisfy the licence.

